Laravel Dox <code>php artisan make:middleware Logger</code> <code>dox create:middleware Logger</code> <code>public function handle(Request $request, Closure $next)</code> <code>dynamic handle(IDoxRequest req)</code> <code>return $next($request);</code> <code>return req;</code> <code>return response('no', 401);</code> <code>return response('no').statusCode(401);</code> <code>abort(404);</code> <code>throw NotFoundHttpException();</code> <code>$middleware-&gt;append(LogMiddleware::class)</code> in <code>bootstrap/app.php</code> <code>AppConfig(globalMiddleware: &lt;dynamic&gt;[LogMiddleware()])</code> lib/app/http/middleware/logger.middleware.dart<pre><code>class LoggerMiddleware implements IDoxMiddleware {
  @override
  dynamic handle(IDoxRequest req) {
    print('${req.method} ${req.uri.path}');
    return req; // go on. anything else is the response.
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>A plain function <code>dynamic apiKey(DoxRequest req)</code> also works as middleware. Dox middleware runs before the controller only. There is no "after" step; use a <code>responseHandler</code> for that.</p>

Laravel Dox <code>php artisan make:request StoreBlogRequest</code> <code>dox create:dto CreateBlog</code> <code>class StoreBlogRequest extends FormRequest</code> with <code>rules()</code> <code>@Dto() class CreateBlog</code> with annotations on <code>final</code> fields <code>'title' =&gt; ['required', 'string', 'max:50']</code> <code>@MaxLength(50) final String title;</code> <code>'age' =&gt; ['nullable', 'integer', 'min:18']</code> <code>@Min(18) final int? age;</code> <code>'email' =&gt; ['required', 'email', 'unique:users']</code> <code>@Email() @Unique('users') final String email;</code> <code>'role' =&gt; Rule::in(['admin', 'user'])</code> <code>final Role role;</code> (a Dart enum) <code>'tags' =&gt; ['array', 'max:5']</code>, <code>'tags.*' =&gt; 'string'</code> <code>@MaxItems(5) final List&lt;String&gt; tags;</code> <code>$request-&gt;validated()</code> the DTO object itself, already typed <code>$request-&gt;validate([...])</code> inside a method <code>await req.validate&lt;CreateBlog&gt;()</code> <code>$request-&gt;input('name')</code> <code>req.input('name')</code> <code>$request-&gt;file('avatar')</code> a <code>RequestFile</code> field in the DTO, or <code>req.input('avatar')</code> <code>$request-&gt;user()</code> <code>req.auth?.user&lt;User&gt;()</code> <code>422</code> with <code>{"errors": {...}}</code> <code>422</code> with a flat map <code>{"email": "...", "items.1.quantity": "..."}</code> lib/app/http/dtos/create_blog.dto.dart<pre><code>@Dto()
